# Security Implementation Rules

<rule>
name: atlas_security
description: Standards for implementing proper security features
filters:
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.(?:js|jsx|ts|tsx|api|json)$"
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?i)security|auth|jwt|token|encrypt|hash|password"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      When implementing security features:

      ## Authentication & Authorization
      - Implement proper JWT handling
      - Use secure session management
      - Implement proper role-based access control
      - Use proper OAuth flows
      - Implement proper token refresh mechanisms

      ## Data Security
      - Implement proper input validation
      - Use proper data sanitization
      - Implement proper CSRF protection
      - Use proper XSS prevention
      - Implement proper SQL injection prevention

      ## API Security
      - Implement proper rate limiting
      - Use proper API key management
      - Implement proper CORS policies
      - Use proper request validation
      - Implement proper error handling

      ## Infrastructure Security
      - Use proper security headers
      - Implement proper CSP policies
      - Use proper HTTPS configuration
      - Implement proper firewall rules
      - Use proper security monitoring

      ## Dependency Security
      - Implement proper dependency scanning
      - Use proper version pinning
      - Implement proper security audits
      - Use proper vulnerability monitoring
      - Implement proper update procedures

examples:
  - input: "Adding a new authentication endpoint"
    output: "Endpoint uses proper JWT handling, input validation, and error handling"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule>